## 6. DEFINITION OF DONE

- [ ] Every phase file exists, with coverage counts reported.
- [ ] Canonical tokens resolve with no nulls, no placeholders, provenance on every leaf.
- [ ] The setup block gets an agent from empty project to one styled component.
- [ ] Zero uses of "appropriate", "consistent", "as needed", "modern" or "clean" as rules.
- [ ] Every SA-6 conflict appears as a ruling in the standard or in `UNRESOLVED.md`.
- [ ] Every image showing a real component is a screenshot of that component.
- [ ] SA-11 built the desk booking app and, on its second run, was forced into no guesses on core foundations.
- [ ] Nothing in the standard is specific to either example project.
- [ ] Drift report delivered separately to the design team.
- [ ] Nothing was modified in Figma, Storybook, or ProGet.

## 7. GUARDRAILS

- Read-only everywhere. Report accidental modifications immediately.
- Every auth wall goes to the human. Never work around one.
- Do not improve the design system while documenting it. Improvements go in the gap list.
- Do not let anti-AI research override house style. Ours wins; log the tension.
- Do not invent brand identity. Flag it.
- Do not summarise a source you could not access. Say you could not access it.
- Do not compress a sub-agent's findings before writing them to disk. Compression happens once, in SA-10.
